 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "boards is a list of non-empty boards; each board is a list of distinct positive integer pins and a pin may appear on several boards. Two pins on a common board are directly connected; relatedness is the transitive closure of direct connection. pin1 and pin2 are distinct positive integers that need not appear on any board (a pin on no board is related to nothing). Variant 2: return the minimum number of boards on a route from pin1 to pin2, where a route is a sequence of boards, the first holding pin1, the last holding pin2, and each consecutive pair sharing a pin (1 when one board holds both); return -1 when the pins are not related.",
